`stdio.h` – Provides standard input and output functions.
`unistd.h` – Provides system functions such as `sleep()`.
`int` – Defines a variable for storing integer values.
`&` – Returns the memory address of a variable.
`%p` – Format specifier used to display memory addresses.
`printf()` – Prints variable values or addresses on the screen.
`while(1)` – Creates a loop that executes continuously.
`sleep(1)` – Pauses program execution for one second.
`gcc` – Compiles C source code into an executable file.
`./filename` – Runs the compiled executable file.
`&` – Executes a program in the background.
`PID` – Unique identification number assigned to each process.
`ASLR` – Address Space Layout Randomization; randomly changes memory addresses to improve security.
`Ctrl + C` – Interrupts and stops the running program.
